1. Added import for ScopeProvider from the scope context
2. Wrapped the NotesIndex component with ScopeProvider
3. The ScopeProvider will use the scope value from the state that's already being managed by useParentState

This should fix the "useScope must be used within a ScopeProvider" error while maintaining the exact functionality of the component. The NotesIndex component will now have access to the scope context it needs.

Note that we're keeping all the original functionality and not creating any mock or simplified version of the component. We're just adding the necessary provider that the component requires to function properly.

